    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The changelog line [ev-9350ba799f1a] is only a title, but the linked PR fills the gap. [ev-721e928a0772] says it is a closed RFC that proposes a new `ExternalArtifact` API, an extension of the `source.toolkit.fluxcd.io` APIs that kustomize-controller and helm-controller can consume. [ev-af979828e17a] shows that the PR's only change is adding the design document rfcs/0012-external-artifact/README.md, which [ev-e55e181b0604] links to. So the subject is the RFC-0012 design document, the change is that the document was added, and the consequence is informational: it changes no runtime code, CLI or manifests, so no environment is exposed. The ExternalArtifact feature itself ships through other entries, such as [ev-649350cce0ab] and [ev-5f2394bf6df0].",
